  "id": "Compound::DB00370 - Gene::153",
  "verbalization": "Mirtazapine is implicated in the interaction with Adrb1 through a series of interconnected molecular and functional pathways. The evidence suggests that Mirtazapine binds to Adra2c, a receptor that participates in multiple biological processes, including Alpha-2a Adrenergic Receptor Binding and Adrenergic Receptor Activity. These processes are ultimately linked to Adrb1, indicating a potential mechanism by which Mirtazapine influences the activity of Adrb1. The shared participation of Adra2c in various receptor-related functions highlights a possible role for Adra2c as a mediator in the interaction between Mirtazapine and Adrb1. The evidence supports a functional link between Mirtazapine and Adrb1, mediated through Adra2c, and underscores the importance of receptor participation in modulating receptor activity.",
